## Detail

### 1. Context and Implementation Overview
Following the cancellation of CRAwDAD Stage V (retrieval on v10, which failed to beat the measured noise floor on `v8`: D 9/30 vs DR 12/30, and cross-seed rerun `crawdad-v8-d3` also scoring 12/30 with 7/30 discordant tasks), this work implements the infrastructure and pre-run specification for **CRAwDAD Grounding v1**.

Grounding evaluates the two standing CRAwDAD small models (`qwen32` = Qwen3-32B Q4_K_M, `r1d32` = DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B Q4_K_M) using execution feedback instead of retrieved memory on the 90 held-out `v10` tasks.

Deliverables produced (all uncommitted in the git worktree `/tmp/wt-ground-v1`, branch `lab/crawdad-ground-v1`):
- [docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/docs/crawdad-ground-v1.md): Pre-run specification document including motivation, the hidden test rule, arm definitions, Stage V pass bar partition, GPU hour estimates, and exact execution commands.
- [README.md](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/README.md#L27): Added a one-line index entry under the Topic docs index matching the standing format.
- [bench/loop/tasks_v10_visible.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/tasks_v10_visible.py): Committed, reviewable mapping of task IDs to visible assert test source strings and check metadata, extracted deterministically on CPU.
- [bench/loop/generate_visible.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/generate_visible.py): Standalone CPU generator that parses prompt "Examples:" sections and builds `tasks_v10_visible.py`.
- [bench/loop/ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/ground.py): Resumable runner CLI supporting `--selftest`, `step`, `status`, and `report [--regrade]`.
- [bench/loop/test_ground.py](file:///tmp/wt-ground-v1/bench/loop/test_ground.py): 14 CPU unit tests verifying all aspects of the grounding loop without model server access.

