### 5. Expected GPU Hours Arithmetic
From measured logs in `docs/crawdad-v8.md` and `docs/crawdad-v10-noise.md` (`crawdad-v8-d2`: 108 replies, decode 24,593 s, mean $\approx 225$ s gen_s per reply, decode generation throughput 10.6–11.2 t/s; model swap $\approx 1.3$ min):
- **Turn 0 (Arm P)**: 180 replies $\times 225\text{ s} = 40,500\text{ s} =$ **11.25 GPU hours** decode.
- **Arm G**:
  - Test-writing: 180 replies $\times 75\text{ s} \approx 13,500\text{ s} =$ 3.75 GPU hours (conservative at 225 s: 11.25 h).
  - Revisions: Worst-case 540 replies = 33.75 GPU hours. Expected case (based on stored v8 solo pass rate $\sim 22\%$, failing pairs average $\sim 1.4$ revisions before early stop): 252 replies $\times 225\text{ s} = 15.75$ GPU hours. Total G expected $\approx$ **19.5 GPU hours** (worst case: **45.0 GPU hours**).
- **Arm C**: Up to 540 revisions. Worst-case: 33.75 GPU hours. Expected case ($\sim 1.2$ revisions before "no changes" stop): 216 replies $\times 225\text{ s} \approx$ **13.5 GPU hours**.
- **Total compute**:
  - **Expected**: P (11.25 h) + G (19.5 h) + C (13.5 h) $\approx$ **44.25 GPU hours** decode.
  - **Worst-case**: P (11.25 h) + G (45.0 h) + C (33.75 h) $=$ **90.0 GPU hours** decode.
- **Session plan**: Exactly 2 llmctl sessions (Session 1: `invite qwen32` running P, G, C for all 90 tasks, `bye`; Session 2: `invite r1d32` running P, G, C for all 90 tasks, `bye`). Model swap overhead $= 2 \times 1.3\text{ min} = 2.6\text{ minutes}$.

